From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:53:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(protocol): complete Bedrock 1.26.60 compatibility

Upstream #466 supplies protocol 2225, its generated assets and the actor
hand fields. Retain the remaining compatibility fixes without duplicating
those changes or replacing the newer upstream player metadata and mappings.

Apply dimension cloud height and visibility through Java 26.3 environment
attributes. Validate signed dimension bounds and reject overflow. Preserve
other dimension attributes when clouds are disabled.

Accept all 57 player UI inventory entries sent by BDS 1.26.60.6. Normalize
legacy block connections without erasing explicit values at the unchanged
block-state version. Retain the native glyphs used by converted packs.

Decode resource-pack response union indexes in the packet codec. Supplement
packet IDs from matching protocol schemas and reject conflicting metadata.
Share outgoing actor swing encoding and retain packet-boundary regressions,
including tests for the passenger codec now supplied by upstream.

Sources: Mojang/bedrock-protocol-docs v1.26.60 (protocol 2225), the matching
1.26.60.5 GDK archive, and the native BDS 1.26.60.6 inventory fixture.
Data Asset Sources records the archive hashes and experimental-data limits.

Decode the optional server presence configuration as one richPresenceId
string. Mojang protocol-2225 presenceConfig metadata has one optional
field. Fresh current Dimension Clash and Treasure Hunt StartGame packets
include that configuration; reading a second string consumes the first
telemetry field and then overruns the packet at ownerId. A boundary
regression preserves the four following telemetry strings with presence
both absent and present. The captured Dimension Clash payload consumes
exactly when decoded with the single presence string. Raw captures remain
private.
